<title>USA: Marathon lowers U.S. posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon lowers U.S. posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective October 1.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.50 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.75 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $22.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
